libbass for Debian
------------------

Sources have been assembled from the un4seen archives (one prebuilt
libbass.so per architecture, bass.h and bass.txt).

The library has no SONAME, and it is not patched: programs linked with -lbass
get "NEEDED libbass.so". debian/libbass2.symbols is therefore keyed on
"libbass.so" and installed by hand in debian/rules, because dh_makeshlibs
ignores libraries without SONAME. The build fails if the exported BASS_*
functions do not match the symbols file: new functions of an upstream update
must be added there with the new version.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

